# Week 1 — Basics of Natural Language Processing (NLP)

## Overview
This week introduces the fundamentals of Natural Language Processing (NLP).  
The focus is on understanding text data, preprocessing techniques, and basic NLP concepts using Python.

---

## Concepts Covered
- What is NLP?
- Tokens, Types, and Corpora
- Text preprocessing techniques:
  - Tokenization
  - Stopword removal
  - Stemming and Lemmatization
- N-grams
- Introduction to NLP libraries

---

## Coding Tasks Implemented
- Tokenization using NLTK
- Stopword removal
- Stemming and lemmatization
- Simple text preprocessing pipeline
- Hands-on practice with real text data

---

## Tools & Libraries Used
- Python
- NLTK
- spaCy
- Google Colab

---

## Key Learnings
- How raw text is converted into machine-readable format
- Importance of preprocessing in NLP pipelines
- Practical usage of NLP libraries

